{"title":"Career Roadmap · Avionics Technician","role":"Avionics Technician","summary":"An Avionics Technician installs, inspects, tests, troubleshoots, maintains and replaces aircraft electronic and electrical systems.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Aircraft Maintenance Engineering (AME - DGCA)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Avionics Technician installs, inspects, tests, troubleshoots, maintains and replaces aircraft electronic and electrical systems."},{"type":"p","text":"The role focuses on aircraft systems such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"Surveillance"},{"text":"Flight instruments"},{"text":"Autopilot"},{"text":"Flight management systems"},{"text":"Aircraft electrical systems"},{"text":"Displays"},{"text":"Radar"},{"text":"Radio systems"},{"text":"Data buses"},{"text":"Sensors"},{"text":"Warning systems"},{"text":"Cabin/entertainment electronics"},{"text":"Aircraft wiring and connectors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong avionics professional combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Aircraft Systems","Electronics","Electrical Engineering","Digital Systems","Communication","Instrumentation","Troubleshooting","Maintenance Documentation","Aviation Safety"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Important qualification note","text":"An aircraft-maintenance-related degree or training does not automatically make a person a licensed/authorized aircraft maintenance professional. In India, DGCA licensing, approved training, experience, aircraft/type-specific requirements and organization authorization can apply depending on the exact maintenance function. The student should verify the current DGCA requirements and the employer's authorization pathway before assuming eligibility for a particular avionics role."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":